{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"toadyish-magic-arrowana","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context / Problem\n\nRP-04's config-ownership drain reaches its final two rows. After C3f\n(`ed65`) drains the nine residual files, `scripts/config_ownership_exceptions.py`\n`LEGACY_EXCEPTIONS` holds exactly TWO rows, both on\n`_engine/rebar_reconciler/binding_lifecycle.py`:\n\n- `RECONCILER_ABSENT_RETIRE_GRACE` — the consecutive-404 absence-retire grace,\n  read in `note_absent` via the local `_env_int` shim.\n- `os.environ.get` — the raw ambient lookup inside that same `_env_int` parser.\n\nBoth were MOVED into `binding_lifecycle.py` from `binding_store.py` by RP-02 S2\n(the absence policy travelled with them). RP-04 S7.3.a (ticket `6633`) closed\nhaving cut the reconciler CORE/JIRA reads but NOT these — its recorded file\nimpact named the pre-move `binding_store.py`, so the moved reads fell through.\nTracker `01d8` records the coupling but is bookkeeping-only (no file impact,\nout of the epic tree). This story is the executable drain that RP-02 S2's move\nleft owing, and it is the LAST one before the whitelist is EMPTY.\n\n## Key finding — the owned accessor already exists\n\nThe cut is NOT a constructor-threading refactor. `src/rebar/_config_sources.py`\n(a composition root that owns env reads) ALREADY exposes\n`resolve_absent_retire_grace()` — \"Owns the read for binding_store/binding_walk\"\n— with byte-identical semantics to the local shim: raw `RECONCILER_ABSENT_RETIRE_GRACE`\nover the default `3`, clamped `>= 1`, malformed/absent → default. The sibling\nreconciler knobs in `fetcher.py`/`applier.py` were cut to `_config_sources`\naccessors the same way (they now carry no ambient reads and no whitelist rows),\nso this is the established, in-process pattern.\n\n## Approach\n\n1. In `binding_lifecycle.py::note_absent`, replace the\n   `_env_int(\"RECONCILER_ABSENT_RETIRE_GRACE\", _DEFAULT_ABSENT_RETIRE_GRACE, minimum=1)`\n   call with `resolve_absent_retire_grace()` imported from `rebar._config_sources`\n   (the same import direction `fetcher.py`/`applier.py` already use — no cycle).\n2. Remove the now-dead `_env_int` helper and the local\n   `_DEFAULT_ABSENT_RETIRE_GRACE` constant from `binding_lifecycle.py` (confirm no\n   other caller first), eliminating the ambient `os.environ.get` read entirely.\n3. Remove BOTH `binding_lifecycle.py` rows from\n   `scripts/config_ownership_exceptions.py`. `LEGACY_EXCEPTIONS` is now EMPTY.\n\n## Portability\n\nThe cut composes through an in-process owned accessor\n(`_config_sources.resolve_absent_retire_grace`); it has no CI-provider or\nexternal-service trigger. The config-ownership gate is a deterministic offline\nAST check. Works with any or no CI provider.\n\n## Outcome / Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `note_absent`'s absence-retire grace is sourced from\n  `_config_sources.resolve_absent_retire_grace()`; no ambient `os.environ` read\n  or `_env_int`-style shim for it remains below the seam in `binding_lifecycle.py`.\n- [ ] The dead `_env_int` helper is removed (no remaining caller), so\n  `binding_lifecycle.py` carries zero below-seam config/credential reads.\n- [ ] Both `binding_lifecycle.py` rows are removed from\n  `scripts/config_ownership_exceptions.py`, and `LEGACY_EXCEPTIONS` is now\n  EMPTY (`[]`) — the whole-tree config-ownership drain is complete.\n- [ ] `python scripts/check_config_ownership.py` reports zero findings with the\n  whitelist empty.\n- [ ] Absence-retire behavior is byte-preserved: default 3, clamp `>= 1`,\n  malformed/absent env → default; a set valid value is honored; a binding\n  retires at exactly `grace` consecutive 404s.","id":"2a95-236b-535f-460e","parent_id":"075b-1479-dcb7-40ab","priority":2,"tags":["reconciler","config","rp04"],"ticket_type":"story","title":"RP-04 C3g: cut binding_lifecycle absence-grace read (reach EMPTY)"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787142001026014001,"uuid":"f045644c-017d-427f-8479-1145621e6675"}